From 166b8be618639ca2ff2b9f34450652d6d932db82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baptiste Coudurier <baptiste.coudurier@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:43:55 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] avformat/mov: prefer the stts duration over mdhd

The media duration can't be shorter than the sample table, so use the
stts sum. This also covers a clipped or missing mdhd duration.

Fixes: #22532
Signed-off-by: Baptiste Coudurier <baptiste.coudurier@gmail.com>

(cherry picked from commit 166b8be618639ca2ff2b9f34450652d6d932db82)
Upstream: https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/166b8be618639ca2ff2b9f34450652d6d932db82
---
 libavformat/mov.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/mov.c b/libavformat/mov.c
index ef99c60..a91ed56 100644
--- a/libavformat/mov.c
+++ b/libavformat/mov.c
@@ -3942,8 +3942,10 @@ static int mov_read_stts(MOVContext *c, AVIOContext *pb, MOVAtom atom)
     }
 
     st->nb_frames= total_sample_count;
+    // The media duration can't be shorter than the sample table, so prefer
+    // the latter when they differ.
     if (duration)
-        st->duration= FFMIN(st->duration, duration);
+        st->duration = duration;
 
     // All samples have zero duration. They have higher chance be chose by
     // mov_find_next_sample, which leads to seek again and again.
